Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: usb: start TX work when a frame is queued

The upper TX worker prepares its initial queue-depth snapshot before
kicking the USB transport. With software encryption, USB submission can
wait for that whole snapshot even though complete frames are queued.

Queue the existing USB worker when admitting each complete frame, under
the same lock and pause gate as the existing kick. Workqueue coalescing
and the existing worker keep submission serialized and aggregate frames
that are available. The final kick and drain/stop paths remain intact.

Not submitted upstream.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/usb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/usb.c
@@ -815,6 +815,8 @@
 		return 0;
 	}
 	skb_queue_tail(&rtwusb->tx_queue[ep], skb);
+	/* Overlap USB submission with preparation of the next TX frames. */
+	queue_work(rtwusb->txwq, &rtwusb->tx_work);
 	spin_unlock_bh(&rtwusb->tx_lock);
 
 	return 0;
